"Production use" means relying on the Software or its results in the
operation of a business, a network or a service.

3. What you may not do

Everything not listed in section 2 requires a licence under section 4. In
particular, without one you may not:

(a) use the Software in production, or for or on behalf of anyone else,
    including by offering it as a hosted or managed service;

(b) distribute, publish, sublicense, sell, rent, lend or otherwise make the
    Software or any modified version of it available to anyone, in whole or
    in part, in source or object form, other than by submitting a
    contribution to the Licensor;

(c) create derivative works of the Software, other than as stated in
    section 2(c);

(d) use the Software or any part of it to develop a product or service that
    competes with it, or to train or evaluate a machine learning model;

(e) remove or alter any copyright, licence or attribution notice.

Where the platform the Software is published on lets its users view or copy
a public repository through the platform's own functions, such as a fork,
that copy stays on the platform, carries this licence, and gives you no
rights beyond section 2.

4. Production use and other further licences

Production use, and any other use beyond section 2, is available on request.
Send the request to the Licensor by e-mail to strata-sec@xmx.starkweb.io.

A further licence exists only once the Licensor has granted it to you in
writing. It covers only the person or organisation, the use, the period and
the conditions, including any fee, that the grant states. The Licensor is
free to refuse a request, to attach conditions to a grant, and to decide
each request differently. A request, a reply that is not a grant, or the
Licensor's silence grants nothing.

Unless the grant says otherwise, a further licence is non-exclusive,
non-transferable and non-sublicensable, and every provision of this licence
that the grant does not expressly replace continues to apply. Where the
grant and this licence conflict, the grant prevails.

